.TH EIC\-PARSE 1 "2026-10-22" "ec2-instance-connect-rh 0.0.1"
.SH NAME
eic\-parse \- verify EC2 Instance Connect signer chain and SSH keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eic\-parse
.B \-p
.I keys_path
.B \-d
.I tmpdir
.B \-s
.I signer_path
.B \-i
.I instance_id
.B \-c
.I expected_cn
.B \-a
.I ca_path
.B \-v
.I ocsp_dir
.RB [ \-f
.IR fingerprint ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B eic\-parse
verifies the EC2 Instance Connect signer certificate trust chain and OCSP
revocation status, then validates each SSH key's signature, timestamp, and
instance ID.
Valid keys are printed to stdout for
.BR sshd (8)
to consume.
.PP
The command is normally called in\-process by
.BR eic\-curl (1)
but can also be run standalone via its CLI interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " keys_path"
Path to the file containing signed SSH keys.
.TP
.BI \-d " tmpdir"
Temporary directory for intermediate files.
.TP
.BI \-s " signer_path"
Path to the PEM file containing the signer certificate chain.
.TP
.BI \-i " instance_id"
Current EC2 instance ID (e.g., i\-1234567890abcdef0).
.TP
.BI \-c " expected_cn"
Expected Common Name of the signer certificate.
.TP
.BI \-a " ca_path"
Path to the CA bundle or CA directory.
.TP
.BI \-v " ocsp_dir"
Directory containing OCSP staple response files.
.TP
.BI \-f " fingerprint"
Optional SSH key fingerprint to match against.
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Valid keys found and printed.
.TP
.B 1
Validation or trust\-chain failure.
.TP
.B 255
No valid keys found.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR eic\-run (1),
.BR eic\-curl (1),
.BR sshd (8),
.BR openssl\-verify (1)
